  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to creating an exemption from certain special assessments, fees and surcharges on hazardous waste generated by or at an elementary or secondary school",
    "basePrintNo": "S5991",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5991-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 36,
       "fullName": "Ruth Hassell-Thompson",
       "imgName": "380_ruth_hassell-thompson.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 380,
       "sessionMemberId": 12,
       "sessionYear": 2009,
       "shortName": "HASSELL-THOMPSON"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §27-0923, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5991\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\ncreating an exemption from certain special assessments, fees and\nsurcharges on hazardous waste generated by or at an elementary or\nsecondary school\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThe purpose of this bill is to exempt elementary and secondary schools\nfrom certain fees resulting from the cleanup of hazardous waste\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis bill would create an exemption from certain special assessments,\nfees and surcharges on hazardous waste generated by or at an\nelementary or secondary school provided that the waste results from\nservices that arc provided:\n\n* under a contract with the Department of Environmental Conservation\n(DEC), the United State Environmental Protection Agency or a court,\nrelated to the cleanup or remediation of a hazardous materials or\nhazardous wastes spill, discharge, or surficial cleanup.\n* under a contract with the DEC for the cleanup and removal of a\npetroleum spill or discharge;\n*under the order of a court, DEC, the Department of Health, or the\nUnited States Environmental Protection Agency, related to an inactive\nhazardous waste disposal site;\n*voluntarily and free of charge; and,\n*under a permit or order requiring corrective action\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nAs more becomes known about the dangers of exposure to environmental\nhazardous like lead and mercury, more and more schools are undertaking\nremediation activities. Hazardous waste cleanup activities at schools\nserve to benefit the safety and health of students. faculty and the\nentire community. This legislation is intended to encourage schools to\nconduct remediation efforts in consultation with the Department of\nEnvironmental Conservation, the Department of Health, or the Untied\nStates Environmental Protection Agency, by providing an exemption from\nhazardous waste special assessments.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nA 11704 of 2008: Passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
